" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244640 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533657 true] [17592186244640 1111 #uuid "893e0416-0e8c-5bd3-92ee-410942e4cb17" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1017 #edb/ref 17592186244642 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1089 "q-122551" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1100 "Mike wants to work out five days a week. In how many ways can Mike choose five days to work out?" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1113 #uuid "e149c852-f83c-539a-9934-97fad19eea16" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1138 false 13194139533657 true] [17592186244641 1145 "The number of combinations of $n$ objects taken $r$ at a time is given by the formula\n\n$$\n{}_{n}{C}_{r}=\\frac{n!}{(n-r)!\\,r!}.\n$$\n\nThere are $7$ days in a week, so $n=7.$ We want to select $5$ of those days for Mike to workout, so we have $r=5.$\n\nTherefore, the number of choices is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{}_{7}{C}_{5} & =\\frac{7!}{(7-5)!\\,5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7!}{2!5!} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6\\cdot \\cancel{5!}}{2!\\cancel{5!}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\cdot 6}{2\\cdot 1} \\\\  & =\\frac{42}{2} \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244643 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244644 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244645 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244646 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1000 #edb/ref 17592186244647 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1041 "selection" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1104 #edb/ref 17592186244644 13194139533657 true] [17592186244642 1110 #uuid "d95e3027-7ce7-55a5-8102-55760b37e356" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244643 1034 "2\\,520" 13194139533657 true] [17592186244643 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533657 true] [17592186244643 1111 #uuid "22f2aed7-e5b0-5356-8cbd-8123be9fd